# app.vigil Testing

## Stack

| Tier | Tool | Helper | Specs |
|------|------|--------|-------|
| Unit | Vitest + `@vue/test-utils` + jsdom | `mountWithPlugins` | co-located `*.spec.ts` |
| Integration | Vitest + `@testing-library/vue` + MSW | `renderWithPlugins` | co-located `*.integration.spec.ts` |
| E2e | Playwright (Chromium) | — | `app.vigil/e2e/` |

- **Run unit + integration**: `cd app.vigil && npm run test:unit:run` (or `make unit`)
- **Run e2e**: `cd app.vigil && npm run test:e2e` (or `make e2e`)
- **Run everything**: `make test-all` (unit + e2e + pest)

## Co-location & versioning

Specs live beside the unit they test (`ALogo.spec.ts` next to `ALogo.vue`).
Every test addition bumps the unit's `RULES.md` `version` and `CHANGELOG.md` top entry to `1.1.0` (SemVer minor).

## Mount helper

```typescript
import { mountWithPlugins } from '@/test/mount';
const wrapper = mountWithPlugins(MyComponent, { props: { ... } });
```

Boots i18n, fresh Pinia, PrimeVue, Toast, ConfirmationService — matches `main.ts`.

For components using `useRoute()`, add a router plugin:

```typescript
import { createRouter, createMemoryHistory } from 'vue-router';
const router = createRouter({ history: createMemoryHistory(), routes: [{ path: '/', component: {} }] });
mountWithPlugins(C, { global: { plugins: [router] } });
```

## PrimeVue stubs

PrimeVue components are NOT auto-imported in Vitest. Stub them in `global.stubs`:

```typescript
stubs: {
  Select: { props: ['modelValue', 'options'], emits: ['update:modelValue'], template: '<div class="select-stub" />' },
  Dialog: { props: ['visible'], emits: ['update:visible'], template: '<div v-if="visible"><slot name="header" /><slot /><slot name="footer" /></div>' },
}
```

## Service / store mocks

```typescript
const getUsers = vi.fn();
vi.mock('../../services', () => ({ GetUsersService: getUsers }));
vi.mock('../../store', () => ({ useUserStore: () => ({ hasPermission: vi.fn() }) }));
// import component AFTER mocks
```

## Async

```typescript
import { flushPromises } from '@vue/test-utils';
getUsers.mockResolvedValue({ data: users });
const wrapper = mountWithPlugins(UsersView, { global: { stubs } });
await flushPromises();
```

## Integration tier — renderWithPlugins (Testing Library + MSW)

Same plugin wiring as `mountWithPlugins` but uses TL's `render()`. Query by role/label/text — **no CSS class queries**. Layout components (`TheLayout`, `ThePageHeader`) are stubbed by default. The component mounts immediately, so set store state **before** render:

```typescript
import { createPinia, setActivePinia } from 'pinia';
import { renderWithPlugins } from '@/test/render';
import { server } from '@/test/msw/server';
import { http, HttpResponse } from 'msw';

const pinia = createPinia();
setActivePinia(pinia);
useUserStore().setUserAndPermissions(mockUser, ['users.read']);

server.use(
  http.get('http://localhost/auth/users', () => HttpResponse.json({ data: users }))
);
renderWithPlugins(UsersView, { pinia, global: { stubs } });

await waitFor(() => expect(screen.getByText('Alice')).toBeInTheDocument());
```

- Default MSW handlers live in `src/test/msw/handlers.ts`; override per-test with `server.use(...)`.
- MSW is wired in `setup.ts` (start before all, reset after each, close after all).
- `vitest.config.ts` sets `VITE_API_URL = 'http://localhost'` so axios builds absolute URLs MSW can intercept.

## Reporter gotcha (terminal wrapper)

The terminal wrapper mangles pretty reporter output — pass counts can read low (e.g. "23" when 24 passed). For trustworthy counts: Vitest → `--reporter=json --outputFile=/tmp/x.json` and parse; Playwright → run from `app.vigil/` (not repo root) with `--reporter=dot`/`--reporter=line`.

## Never-commit rule

A spec is **done** only after a green run confirmed by the human. Do not commit unrun specs.
